module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- queries = solve ∘ materialize — the MATERIALIZE half + the four query
-- entries. expr-substrate Phase 16 (brief:
-- `workstreams/expr-substrate/briefs/phase-16-queries-materialize.md`).
--
-- P13 (`solveRel`/`solveFnRel`) shipped the relational solve over a THREADED
-- facts env — the pure core NEVER fetches; the caller builds `{ relations,
-- rules }`. P15 (`solveRelAll`/`solveFnRelAll` + `relSolveSet`) shipped the
-- findall family (EVERY satisfying binding). What was missing is ONLY the
-- bridge: entity-instance rows → relation extensions. This phase ships that
-- bridge (the pure builders) + the four query entries (thin compositions over
-- the SHIPPED solve+findall families). NOT new reasoning.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- THE relDef MARKER (caller-facing; the `$`-key barrier discipline — a Fenel
-- body can't author `$`-keyed objects, so the input is a plain record, same as
-- the facts env in rel-solve.fenel):
--   relDef = { name        — the atom-head spelling the query lambda uses
--                            (caller's choice, VERBATIM — the P13 rule)
--            , fieldOrder   — the projection column names IN ORDER (THREADED by
--                            the caller; deriving it from the `$`-keyed entity
--                            schema is a TS-boundary / exposure-era job, NOT a
--                            pure-body job)
--            , instances }  — the flat merged-envelope rows
--                            `{ id, accountId, ...data, createdAt, updatedAt }`
--                            that `state:listInstancesByName` returns (storage
--                            strips the top-level `$tag`; variant values NESTED
--                            in fields keep theirs).
--
-- ENVELOPE FIELDS ARE ORDINARY COLUMNS (decision 2): `id` / `accountId` /
-- `createdAt` / `updatedAt` sit flat in the row exactly like data fields —
-- `fieldOrder` decides what projects. NO special-casing: an `id`-join
-- (`ownerOf x y` where `y` is an instance id) is a first-class query shape.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- THE BUILDERS:
--   • projectInstanceRow fieldOrder instance ⇒ Maybe row — `std:lookup` each
--     name in order; ANY missing field ⇒ Nothing (the row is dropped upstream
--     — a fact must be TOTAL; partial rows can't join honestly. The proven-rows
--     spirit: we only assert facts we fully read).
--   • rowsFromInstances fieldOrder instances ⇒ rows — fold, dropping Nothing.
--   • relationFromInstances name fieldOrder instances ⇒ { name, arity, rows }.
--   • relDefToRelation / relationsFromDefs / factsFromDefs ⇒ the facts env.
--
-- SCALAR CELLS MATCH; VARIANT CELLS RIDE BUT DON'T MATCH (decision 4 — the
-- shallow-eq honesty fence). std `eq` is reference-shallow on records (the P13
-- rowEq rationale; Step-0 probe re-confirmed: `eq {tag=Just,_0=5} {tag=Just,
-- _0=5}` ⇒ false), so a variant-valued cell (`{$tag:"Just",_0:5}` nested in a
-- field) projects into rows VERBATIM via std:lookup but a constant/residual
-- match against it is `false` — the row simply never matches, sound-by-under-
-- approximation (proven-rows). Deep structural matching is a documented
-- widening (a cross-surface deep-eq discipline decision), NOT this phase.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- THE FOUR QUERY ENTRIES — thin compositions, findall-first (decision 3):
--   queryRel       expr relDefs rules                  = solveRelAll over the env
--   queryRelOne    expr relDefs rules                  = solveRel (first-witness)
--   queryFnRel     input ctorDefs nullValue relDefs rules = solveFnRelAll (reify)
--   queryFnRelOne  input ctorDefs nullValue relDefs rules = solveFnRel (reify)
-- All semantics INHERITED: `Just []` = safe-but-empty, `Nothing` = fence/unsafe
-- (the P15 split), proven-rows residuals, stage-1 fences. solve/solveFn/solveRel
-- /solveFnRel/solveRelAll/solveFnRelAll/relSolveSet/enumerateSet/inhabit
-- ALL stay byte-untouched.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- THE LIVE CALLER (documented, NOT wired here — decision 6). A production
-- `state:queryRel` (requires HasStateIO, body calling `engine:factsFromDefs`)
-- DANGLES today: engine ∉ SYSTEM_MODULES, so the cross-module refs don't
-- resolve in the production registry. The live wiring is therefore the
-- caller-side one-liner:
--   listInstancesByName "Customer"   -- the ONE storage leaf (state.ts:876)
--     |> \rows -> { name = "customer", fieldOrder = ["id", "boughtBook", "joinedDay"], instances = rows }
--     |> \relDef -> dispatchedQueryRel queryExpr [relDef] []
-- demonstrated in materialize.test.ts with HANDLER-SHAPED fixture rows. The
-- production query surface rides the engine→SYSTEM_MODULES exposure decision
-- (the parked P5-era item) + the state-module orchestration fn that lands with
-- it — NOT this phase.
--
-- NO ENTITY DECLS / NO Enumerable/Queryable typeclass (decision 7): relDefs +
-- facts + rows are plain records (the audit-green invariant) ⇒ codename-lock
-- +0, law +0, entity oracle untouched, audit exit-0.
-- =========================================================================

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- projectInstanceRow — `std:lookup` each fieldOrder name in order; ANY missing
-- field ⇒ Nothing (the row must be TOTAL).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Project instance row"
@description "Project one flat merged-envelope instance row onto a fieldOrder column list ⇒ Maybe row (a positional scalar list in column order). `std:lookup` each name in order; ANY missing field ⇒ Nothing — the row is dropped upstream (a fact must be TOTAL; partial rows can't join honestly — the proven-rows spirit: only facts we fully read are asserted). Envelope fields (id / accountId / createdAt / updatedAt) project exactly like data fields — fieldOrder decides what projects. A variant-valued cell rides verbatim under Just (decision 4 — it projects but never matches a constant, by std eq's reference-shallowness). expr-substrate Phase 16."
@tags "engine" "query" "materialize" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
projectInstanceRow : (fieldOrder: List String) -> (instance: a) -> Maybe a
projectInstanceRow fieldOrder instance =
  projectFields fieldOrder instance []

@label "Project fields"
@description "The fold behind projectInstanceRow: walk a fieldOrder name list, `std:lookup` each on the instance, appending its value to the row; the first missing key short-circuits to Nothing (the total-row requirement). Empty / exhausted names ⇒ Just acc. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "query" "materialize" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
@category "engine-internal"
projectFields : (names: a) -> (instance: a) -> (acc: a) -> Maybe a
projectFields names instance acc =
  case head names of
    Nothing -> Just acc
    Just n ->
      case lookup instance n of
        Nothing -> Nothing
        Just v ->
          let rest = case tail names of
                       Nothing -> []
                       Just r -> r
          projectFields rest instance (appendItem v acc)

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- rowsFromInstances — fold the instances, dropping Nothing (partial) rows.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Rows from instances"
@description "Materialize a relation's EXTENSION from a flat merged-envelope instance list: projectInstanceRow each, KEEPING only the total (Just) rows — a partial instance (missing a fieldOrder column) is silently dropped (the proven-rows / total-fact policy). The positional rows feed straight into the P13 facts env. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "query" "materialize" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
@category "engine-internal"
rowsFromInstances : (fieldOrder: a) -> (instances: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
rowsFromInstances fieldOrder instances acc =
  case head instances of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just inst ->
      let acc2 = case projectInstanceRow fieldOrder inst of
                   Just row -> appendItem row acc
                   Nothing -> acc
      case tail instances of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> rowsFromInstances fieldOrder rest acc2

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- relationFromInstances / relDefToRelation / relationsFromDefs / factsFromDefs
-- — assemble the P13 facts env from relDef markers + rules.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Relation from instances"
@description "Build a P13 relation entry `{ name, arity, rows }` from a name, a fieldOrder, and a flat instance list. `name` = the atom-head spelling the query lambda uses (caller's choice, verbatim); `arity` = length fieldOrder; `rows` = the materialized total-row extension (rowsFromInstances). expr-substrate Phase 16."
@tags "engine" "query" "materialize" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
relationFromInstances : (name: String) -> (fieldOrder: a) -> (instances: a) -> a
relationFromInstances name fieldOrder instances =
  { name = name, arity = length fieldOrder, rows = rowsFromInstances fieldOrder instances [] }

@label "Rel def to relation"
@description "Materialize one relDef marker `{ name, fieldOrder, instances }` into a P13 relation entry `{ name, arity, rows }` (relationFromInstances over its three fields). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "query" "materialize" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
@category "engine-internal"
relDefToRelation : (relDef: a) -> a
relDefToRelation relDef =
  relationFromInstances relDef.name relDef.fieldOrder relDef.instances

@label "Relations from defs"
@description "Map a relDef-marker list onto the P13 relations list (relDefToRelation each), threading the accumulator. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "query" "materialize" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
@category "engine-internal"
relationsFromDefs : (relDefs: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
relationsFromDefs relDefs acc =
  case head relDefs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just rd ->
      let acc2 = appendItem (relDefToRelation rd) acc
      case tail relDefs of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> relationsFromDefs rest acc2

@label "Facts from defs"
@description "Assemble the P13 facts env `{ relations, rules }` from a relDef-marker list + a pre-reified rules list: materialize every relDef into a relation extension (relationsFromDefs), pass the rules through verbatim (each `{ name, params, body }`, body PRE-REIFIED to Expr by the caller). The bridge between the entity-instance world and the relational solver. expr-substrate Phase 16."
@tags "engine" "query" "materialize" "datalog" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
factsFromDefs : (relDefs: a) -> (rules: a) -> a
factsFromDefs relDefs rules =
  { relations = relationsFromDefs relDefs [], rules = rules }

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- The four query entries — thin compositions over the SHIPPED solve+findall
-- families (decision 3). findall-first.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Query relational"
@description "queries = solve ∘ materialize (the findall entry): materialize relDef markers + rules into the P13 facts env (factsFromDefs), then enumerate ALL satisfying bindings of a multi-binder predicate `Expr` (solveRelAll over collectFreeVars order) ⇒ Maybe (List bindings). THE engine-side query primitive: a user query ('bought book B ∧ joined < 3 days') = a predicate over materialized entity-instance relations. `Just []` = query SAFE but no satisfying rows; `Nothing` = unsafe / out-of-fragment (the inherited P15 split). The production exposure (a `state:queryRel` orchestration fn calling the live `listInstancesByName → relDef`) rides the engine→SYSTEM_MODULES decision (decision 6). expr-substrate Phase 16."
@tags "engine" "query" "materialize" "solve" "relational" "datalog" "prover" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
queryRel : (expr: Expr) -> (relDefs: a) -> (rules: a) -> Maybe a
queryRel expr relDefs rules =
  solveRelAll expr (factsFromDefs relDefs rules)

@label "Query relational one"
@description "The first-witness sibling of queryRel: materialize relDef markers + rules into the facts env, then solveRel (the first satisfying binding) ⇒ Maybe (List binding). `Nothing` = unsafe / out-of-fragment / no satisfying row (solveRel folds safe-but-empty back to Nothing via witTuples-on-empty — the P13 first-witness behaviour). expr-substrate Phase 16."
@tags "engine" "query" "materialize" "solve" "relational" "datalog" "prover" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
queryRelOne : (expr: Expr) -> (relDefs: a) -> (rules: a) -> Maybe a
queryRelOne expr relDefs rules =
  solveRel expr (factsFromDefs relDefs rules)

@label "Query fn relational"
@description "The reify-composed findall query entry: materialize relDef markers + rules into the facts env, then solveFnRelAll (reify the marshalled Fn value to its Expr body + captures, the lambda's PARAMS as the ordered unknowns) ⇒ EVERY satisfying binding. The lambda form of queryRel — `\\x y -> and (boughtBook x \"book-b\") (joinedDay y) ...`. reify's Err (bodyless / native) ⇒ Nothing; safe-but-empty ⇒ Just []; unsafe ⇒ Nothing. expr-substrate Phase 16."
@tags "engine" "query" "materialize" "solve" "relational" "reify" "datalog" "prover" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
queryFnRel : (input: { body: a, params: List String, env: a }) -> (ctorDefs: a) -> (nullValue: a) -> (relDefs: a) -> (rules: a) -> Maybe a
queryFnRel input ctorDefs nullValue relDefs rules =
  solveFnRelAll input ctorDefs nullValue (factsFromDefs relDefs rules)

@label "Query fn relational one"
@description "The reify-composed first-witness query entry: materialize relDef markers + rules into the facts env, then solveFnRel (reify, the params as the ordered unknowns, the FIRST satisfying binding) ⇒ Maybe (List binding). The lambda form of queryRelOne. reify's Err ⇒ Nothing; no satisfying row ⇒ Nothing. expr-substrate Phase 16."
@tags "engine" "query" "materialize" "solve" "relational" "reify" "datalog" "prover" "expr-substrate" "phase-16"
queryFnRelOne : (input: { body: a, params: List String, env: a }) -> (ctorDefs: a) -> (nullValue: a) -> (relDefs: a) -> (rules: a) -> Maybe a
queryFnRelOne input ctorDefs nullValue relDefs rules =
  solveFnRel input ctorDefs nullValue (factsFromDefs relDefs rules)
